/-
Johnson/Desc/ProofFile/Honest/K4/Law/ExchangeOfTies.lean: CONDITIONAL: on the library's hypothesis h
on the public files and on every hypothesis named. THE FULL SIZE ALONE.

What is here. The thread's debt `ExchangeAtS` at the own item of the member of the feed-forward
layers' own rounds (sub-protocol K4), at the thread with the library's own values (`lettersHead`,
Honest/Thread/FirstHead.lean), WITH NO HYPOTHESIS ON A STATE BEHIND THE MEMBER's STEP:
`k4_exchange_of_b1` (Law/ExchangeOfB1.lean) with its hypothesis hR had from `k4JoinB1_head`
(Law/JoinB1AtHead.lean), which asks one tie more wherever the thread stands (hW), and its
hypothesis hA from `matsAre_head` (Law/W/MatsAreHead.lean). Nothing new is shown: one call.

  `k4_exchange_of_ties`   **`ExchangeAtS T Said k (Item.formsT m 3 "own")`.**

Not shown here. b1 (the field b1 of `JoinB1At`, Law/W/JoinLeftB1.lean), THE LOOKUP's OWN SENTENCE,
WHICH HOLDS ALL THE CONTENT THAT IS LEFT OF THE BATCHED SUMCHECK's OWN CLAIM, IS MOVED, NOT SHOWN:
`k4JoinB1_head` has it out of a clause of `ThrS`: the sentence of the thread's open item on the
keys' worth, which is owed behind the member of the lookup on the calls; no file of K4's honest
side ends in it, and the head of Law/W/JoinB1Head.lean says what whoever shows it must show. What
the public item `.left m` says beside its test is spent likewise. SO THE CONCLUSION SPEAKS ONLY
WHERE A THREAD STANDS THAT HOLDS THESE ALREADY. NO BINDER NAMES A STATE BEHIND THE STEP; but three
of them (hMask, hc, hW) speak of the witness at every continuation of the challenges heard, those
of the step and behind it among them, and so does the thread's clause. hW (`K4LayersTieAt`,
Law/W/LayersTie.lean): the layers' matrices that the lookup's caller reads off the witness are
those of the input's weights: a hypothesis on the thread's Script and on the private input's
weights, asked at every number l of a layer, without a bound: where the library's layerR reads
outside the table of weights it is a sentence on the input's reader there, which a reader that is 0
there meets and another may fail; that an honest Script and a valid input meet it is not shown. HAD
ELSEWHERE, NOT CALLED HERE: hW from one hypothesis under Vd (`layersTie_thr`,
Law/W/LayersOfIndex.lean); hiW from the same (`hiW_of_index`, Law/W/IndexHiW.lean); hTokP at the
lot's own reader of the tokens (`hTokP_of_fine`, Law/W/TokOfFine.lean); hL at the look k4LookAt
(`k4LookAt_head`, Law/LookAtHead.lean); hx (`layAt_laid`, Law/W/LayAtHead.lean: it is asked here
because hW names xl); hQ (`k4Pub_head`, Law/FrontCount.lean); Lh (`laid_head`,
Law/SeatedHead.lean); fits from `fits_member` (Law/FitsMember.lean) with `lookFits_lookAt`
